  "id": "Compound::DB00959 - Gene::2908",
  "verbalization": "Methylprednisolone is linked to Nr3c1 through a series of biological pathways that involve glucocorticoid receptor activation. The evidence suggests that Methylprednisolone, as a corticosteroid hormone receptor agonist, binds to Nr3c1, which is a key component of the glucocorticoid receptor complex. This binding is supported by multiple paths, including direct interactions between Methylprednisolone and Nr3c1, as well as indirect pathways through the 21-hydroxy steroid and therapeutic glucocorticoid classes. The presence of multiple low common ancestors, such as 21-hydroxy steroid and therapeutic glucocorticoid, reinforces the shared biochemical context of these compounds. The consistent involvement of Prednisolone in causing effects like myocardial rupture and alkalosis hypokalaemia further underscores the role of glucocorticoid receptors in these processes. The integration of these pathways highlights the central role of Nr3c1 in mediating the effects of glucocorticoids, with Methylprednisolone acting as a direct agonist in this context.",
